11. The Human Enters the Machine

Eventually the moment arrives that no AI system can perform on the brothers’ behalf.

Someone must climb aboard.

The engine starts.

The propellers turn.

The machine begins travelling along the rail.

There is uncertainty.

There is risk.

There is no simulation capable of converting the final unknown into certainty.

The aircraft either flies or it doesn’t.

This is the boundary between analysis and action.

And it exposes an important limitation.

An AI can calculate the wing.

It can simulate the airflow.

It can identify the structural weakness.

It can analyse the propeller.

It can optimise the engine.

It can examine the evidence.

It can suggest tests.

It can find mistakes.

But eventually someone has to get in the fucking aeroplane.

