16. Discussion

The central problem is not that AI systems identify risk.

Identifying risk is useful.

The problem occurs when:

[
\text{Identify constraint}
]

silently becomes:

[
\text{Change objective}
]

without permission from the person actually responsible for the project.

These are fundamentally different operations.

A competent engineering assistant says:

“Your wing spar fails at 4.7g.”

An incompetent paternalistic assistant says:

“Because the wing spar fails at 4.7g, I have redesigned the aircraft as a train.”

The first answer expands human capability.

The second replaces human judgement.

