17. The Innovation Bubble

This also illuminates a contradiction at the centre of the contemporary AI boom.

The industry promises machines capable of giving individuals productive capabilities previously available only to corporations, universities and governments.

One person will supposedly gain access to:

* engineers,
* programmers,
* mathematicians,
* researchers,
* lawyers,
* designers,
* analysts,
* scientists,
* project managers,
* and technical writers.

This would represent an extraordinary redistribution of productive capacity.

But there is a catch.

If every one of these simulated experts possesses the personality of the organisation’s most nervous compliance department, the individual has not received a laboratory.

They have received a committee.

